## Maintenance Mode

Lament has a database-driven maintenance mode that can be toggled per service.

### Enable Maintenance

```bash
curl -X PUT \
  -H "X-Master-Key: your_key" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"lament_api": true, "lament": true, "description": "Scheduled maintenance"}' \
  https://api.lament.rynds.my.id/maintenance
```

### Disable Maintenance

```bash
curl -X PUT \
  -H "X-Master-Key: your_key" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"lament_api": false, "lament": false, "description": ""}' \
  https://api.lament.rynds.my.id/maintenance
```

### Behavior

When `lament_api` is `true`:
- All API endpoints (except `/health`, `/ping`, `/maintenance`) return `503`
- The response includes a maintenance description and timestamp
- The bypass can be enabled with `BYPASS_MAINTENANCE=true` env var

When `lament` is `true`:
- The SvelteKit frontend redirects users to a maintenance page
- The redirect is handled in `hooks.server.ts`

## Repair Scripts

The scraper includes several repair scripts:

```bash
bun run repair            # Repair metadata
bun run repair:audio      # Repair audio files
bun run repair:title      # Repair track titles
bun run repair:tracks     # Repair track images
```
